PIN ABOVE DESK · USE BEFORE ANY NEW BUILD, AUTOMATION, OR RESEARCH READ

**The 30-Second Test**

| **Does this carry real load — or is the building itself the calm?** |
| --- |

| **LOAD-BEARING** Carries weight the system needs. Without it, substrate, infrastructure, or income visibly degrades. **SIGNS** Names a specific user, customer, or lane it serves Failure mode is concrete — X breaks if this doesn't ship The work to add it is annoying, not relieving |  | **ACTIVATION** The building is what makes the substrate calm enough to function. Legitimate. Just not load-bearing. **SIGNS** “I'll figure out where it fits later” Spec'd to higher precision than current need requires Drafting the architecture feels better than the deploy |
| --- | --- | --- |

**THE VERDICT**

**Load-bearing → **build it. No guilt.

**Activation → **fine. But name it. Don't ship it as infrastructure.

**Can****'****t tell → **it's activation. Treat it that way until the load shows up.

